PS4 text dialog adapter, 2026-10-03:
  source/emulator/src/Libs/LibSceImeDialog.cpp adapts the host editor and
  lifecycle in source/gen4/gen5/compatibility/src/libs/imeCommon.cpp and imeDialog.cpp.
  The imported implementation remains GPL-2.0-only at the PS5 pin above.
  The original PS4 adapter validates guest memory and uses host-owned text;
  the historical import was made in the derivative, now held in this checkout.
  The desktop panel links the imported Dear ImGui SDL2/SDLRenderer2 backends
  (MIT, copyright 2014-2026 Omar Cornut). Their pin and complete license are
  preserved in source/gen4/gen5/UPSTREAM.json and
  source/gen4/gen5/compatibility/3rdparty/imgui/LICENSE.txt. The panel layout is original
  Lumen code; no PS5 graphics engine or controller implementation is linked.

Android SDL text bridge, 2026-10-03:
  SDL_androidtext.h and SDLTextInputCommit.java are original Lumen additions
  licensed GPL-2.0-only. Modified SDL Android C/Java files retain their
  original SDL zlib notices and identify the local changes. These additions
  validate Unicode and preserve text/Return ordering for the shared editor.

Shared host keyboard panels, 2026-10-03:
  source/shared/ime/KeyboardPanel and RuntimeImeDialogUi.java are original
  Lumen GPL-2.0-only UI code shared by the PS4 and PS5 frontends. They use
  owned host snapshots and typed host actions, never guest memory pointers.
  PS5 keeps its existing SDL3/ImGui presentation and IME owner arbitration;
  the PS4 desktop keeps its separate SDL2 software window. Core PS5 full
  text replacements remain queued until the guest invokes ImeUpdate.
  Dear ImGui and SDL retain the component notices and licenses above.

