Selectable QEMU TCG CPU provider, 2026-10-04:
  The original common provider, C execution boundary, build recipes and
  selector are Lumen GPL-2.0-only additions under source/cpu. They embed the
  CPU/TCG closure of QEMU 11.1.2, choosing GPL version 2 where upstream
  offers that choice. QEMU's per-file licenses, including LGPL and permissive
  components, remain applicable. The official archive pin and its SHA-256
  are recorded in source/cpu/qemu/source-lock.json; dependency archive and
  checked local patch pins are in dependency-lock.json. Local QEMU patches
  retain the licenses of their upstream files. No firmware, ROM, guest OS
  or third-party machine image is included in this provider.
  The native build recipes retain QEMU, GLib, PCRE2 and libintl notices.
  Android additionally retains toolchain notices and actual compiled/header
  source preambles. Android builds containing the provider package these
  materials under Legal/QEMU-TCG
  and verify their manifest against the selected native binary. Static
  dependency linkage does not remove the applicable corresponding-source
  and relinking obligations. These pins and notices do not certify a public
  binary distribution; the actual closure must be assessed with the rest
  of Lumen before a release.
